WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.788
A faster algorithm

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.298
for extracting hexadecimal

00:00:03.109 --> 00:00:04.194
digits of π

00:00:04.734 --> 00:00:06.160
Robert Smith presents

00:00:06.043 --> 00:00:07.587
a rearranged Euler-derived

00:00:07.399 --> 00:00:08.802
series for extracting

00:00:08.614 --> 00:00:09.509
hex digits of

00:00:09.321 --> 00:00:10.877
π without computing

00:00:10.689 --> 00:00:11.703
earlier digits

00:00:11.995 --> 00:00:13.705
using about 61%

00:00:13.517 --> 00:00:14.695
fewer divisions and

00:00:14.519 --> 00:00:16.158
38% fewer full

00:00:15.969 --> 00:00:17.608
modular exponentiations

00:00:17.432 --> 00:00:18.717
than Huvent's eight-term

00:00:18.528 --> 00:00:19.294
formula

00:00:19.822 --> 00:00:21.001
The method competes

00:00:20.813 --> 00:00:21.732
with the classic

00:00:21.544 --> 00:00:22.840
Bailey-Borwein-Plouffe

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:24.149
Bellard and Huvent

00:00:23.961 --> 00:00:25.694
digit-extraction formulas

00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:27.436
Collecting the series'

00:00:27.248 --> 00:00:28.155
terms by odd

00:00:27.967 --> 00:00:29.700
denominator 2k +

00:00:29.536 --> 00:00:30.620
1 lets four

00:00:30.432 --> 00:00:31.611
remainders share one

00:00:31.422 --> 00:00:32.130
division

00:00:32.319 --> 00:00:33.038
and the gaps

00:00:32.849 --> 00:00:33.781
between the terms

00:00:33.592 --> 00:00:34.889
mean those remainders

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.337
don't have to

00:00:35.149 --> 00:00:36.658
be computed independently

00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:37.047
either

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:38.344
cutting the operation

00:00:38.156 --> 00:00:38.757
count

00:00:39.294 --> 00:00:40.308
Full story on

00:00:40.119 --> 00:00:41.015
the dashboard
